v1.0 Goals
==========================================

A small but coherent “society” of Abstractors that can take a 
stream of synthetic (or simple real) images containing an 
approaching stop sign and reliably produce a high-level 
StopSignDetected Abstraction.

The system should demonstrate several emergent behaviors 
working together in one integrated scenario:

1. Object tracking with identity — The system maintains a persistent 
   track of the object across frames even as it grows and moves.

2. Focus of attention / suppression — Low-level detectors stop 
   redundantly reporting the same object once it is being tracked.

3. Incremental evidence accumulation — Recognition improves over 
   multiple frames as more evidence (size, shape, color, position) 
   becomes available.

4. Multi-level feature combination — Mid-level Abstractors combine 
   simpler features (e.g., red region + octagonal shape) into 
   higher-level hypotheses.

5. Good observability — The logging and tracing make it reasonably 
   clear why the system eventually fires StopSignDetected.



This is not a production-grade vision system. It is a research/experimental 
milestone that shows the architecture can produce meaningful emergent behavior 
on a concrete, understandable task.


